This directory contains scripts which simulate a variety of reversible
logic circuits with and without errors and error correction. All of
these simulations use the density matrix representation.  Please see
our related paper which can be found at
http://arxiv.org/abs/quant-ph/0403114

The functionality of the 9sym and ham15 circuits comes from
"Reversible Logic Synthesis Benchmarks Page"
(http://www.cs.uvic.ca/~dmaslov/)

Scripts
-------

9sym1.qpro: A reversible logic circuit which outputs a |1> on the
	    final qubit if the number of |1>'s in the input qubits is
	    3, 4, 5, or 6.  The input qubits are initialized to
	    contain 3 |1>'s.

9sym2.qpro: A reversible logic circuit which outputs a |1> on the
	    final qubit if the number of |1>'s in the input qubits is
	    3, 4, 5, or 6.  The input qubits are initialized to
	    contain 4 |1>'s.

9sym3.qpro: A reversible logic circuit which outputs a |1> on the
	    final qubit if the number of |1>'s in the input qubits is
	    3, 4, 5, or 6.  The input qubits are initialized to
	    contain 5 |1>'s.

9sym4.qpro: A reversible logic circuit which outputs a |1> on the
	    final qubit if the number of |1>'s in the input qubits is
	    3, 4, 5, or 6.  The input qubits are initialized to
	    contain 6 |1>'s.

9sym5.qpro: A reversible logic circuit which outputs a |1> on the
	    final qubit if the number of |1>'s in the input qubits is
	    3, 4, 5, or 6.  The input qubits are initialized to
	    contain 7 |1>'s.

hadder_bf1.qpro: A reversible half-adder that uses qubits encoded in
		 the 7-qubit CSS code.  A bit-flip error is simulated
		 on the third physical qubit of the first logical
		 qubit.  This error is detected and corrected.
		 Finally, the behavior of the half-adder is checked
		 after the error is corrected.

hadder_bf2.qpro: A reversible half-adder that uses qubits encoded in
		 the 7-qubit CSS code.  A bit-flip error is simulated
		 on the fifth physical qubit of the first logical
		 qubit.  This error is detected and corrected.
		 Finally, the behavior of the half-adder is checked
		 after the error is corrected.

hadder_bf3.qpro: A reversible half-adder that uses qubits encoded in
		 the 7-qubit CSS code.  A bit-flip error is simulated
		 on the seventh physical qubit of the first logical
		 qubit.  This error is detected and corrected.
		 Finally, the behavior of the half-adder is checked
		 after the error is corrected.

hadder_pf1.qpro: A reversible half-adder that uses qubits encoded in
		 the 7-qubit CSS code.  A phase-flip error is
		 simulated on the third physical qubit of the first
		 logical qubit.  This error is detected and corrected.
		 Finally, the behavior of the half-adder is checked
		 after the error is corrected.

hadder_pf2.qpro: A reversible half-adder that uses qubits encoded in
		 the 7-qubit CSS code.  A phase-flip error is
		 simulated on the fifth physical qubit of the first
		 logical qubit.  This error is detected and corrected.
		 Finally, the behavior of the half-adder is checked
		 after the error is corrected.

hadder_pf3.qpro: A reversible half-adder that uses qubits encoded in
		 the 7-qubit CSS code.  A phase-flip error is
		 simulated on the seventh physical qubit of the first
		 logical qubit.  This error is detected and corrected.
		 Finally, the behavior of the half-adder is checked
		 after the error is corrected.

ham15_1.qpro: A reversible logic circuit implementation of the size 15
	      Hamming optimal coding function.  The input to this
	      circuit is 100100101010001.

ham15_2.qpro: A reversible logic circuit implementation of the size 15
	      Hamming optimal coding function.  The input to this
	      circuit is 111101001010101.

ham15_3.qpro: A reversible logic circuit implementation of the size 15
	      Hamming optimal coding function.  The input to this
	      circuit is 001010001000101.

rc_adder1.qpro: A 16-qubit reversible ripple carry adder which can
		perform the addition of 4-bit numbers.  This circuit
		computes 14 + 5.

rc_adder2.qpro: A 16-qubit reversible ripple carry adder which can
		perform the addition of 4-bit numbers.  This circuit
		computes 2 + 11.

rc_adder3.qpro: A 16-qubit reversible ripple carry adder which can
		perform the addition of 4-bit numbers.  This circuit
		computes 15 + 15.

rc_adder4.qpro: A 16-qubit reversible ripple carry adder which can
		perform the addition of 4-bit numbers.  This circuit
		computes 4 + 5.
